As we know that, if f(2a - x) = f(x) then \(\rm \int_{0}^{2a}f(x)dx=2\int_{0}^{a}f(x)dx\) 
​\(\Rightarrow \rm \int_{0}^{2\pi}{{\cos x}}\;dx = 2\int_{0}^{\pi}{{\cos x}}\;dx = 2\left[ {\sin x} \right]_{0}^{\pi } = 0\)​
Hence, option A is correct.$fix$
